hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1009.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abdullah ibn Abbas that Sad ibn Ubada questioned the Messenger of Allah"
"1009.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Masud from Abdullah ibn Abbas that Sad ibn Ubada questioned the Messenger of Allah"
"1010.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that his paternal aunt related that her grandmother made a vow to walk to the Quba mosque. She died"
"1010.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr that his paternal aunt related that her grandmother made a vow to walk to the Quba mosque. She died"
"1011.1","Do not kill women or children or an
aged, infirm person. Do not cut down fruit-bearing trees. Do not
destroy an inhabited place. Do not slaughter sheep or camels except
for food. Do not burn bees and do not scatter them. Do not steal from
the booty, and do not be cowardly."""
"1011.2","Do not kill women or children or an
aged, infirm person. Do not cut down fruit-bearing trees. Do not
destroy an inhabited place. Do not slaughter sheep or camels except
for food. Do not burn bees and do not scatter them. Do not steal from
the booty, and do not be cowardly."""
"1012.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Urwa ibn Udhayna al-Laythi said"
"1012.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Urwa ibn Udhayna al-Laythi said"
"1013","[1013] And he told me on the authority of Malik that he had heard that Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman used to say: Like the saying of Abdullah bin Omar. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1013 Arabic Hadith:"
"1014.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"1014.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"1015.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that what he preferred of what he had heard from the people of knowledge about a man or woman who vowed to walk to the House of Allah"
"1015.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that what he preferred of what he had heard from the people of knowledge about a man or woman who vowed to walk to the House of Allah"
"1016.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say"
"1016.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say"
"1017.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Talha ibn Abi al-Malik al- Ayli from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn as-Siddiq from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah"
"1017.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Talha ibn Abi al-Malik al- Ayli from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn as-Siddiq from A'isha that the Messenger of Allah"
"1018.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"1018.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"1019.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1019.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1020.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1020.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1021.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah from Abu Muhammad, the mawla of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah ibn Rib'i that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Hunayn. When we met, the Muslims had a setback (jawlah). He said: I saw a man from the polytheists overpowering a man from the Muslims. He said: I turned around for him until I came upon him from behind, and I struck him with the sword on the shoulder blade. He turned to me and embraced me, and I found from that embrace the smell of death. Then death overtook him and he released me. He said: Then I met Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: ""What is the matter with the people?"" He said: ""Allah's command."" Then the people returned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever kills a slain person and has proof of it, his spoils (salab) are for him."" He said: I stood up, then said: ""Who will witness for me?"" Then I sat down. Then he said: ""Whoever kills a slain person and has proof of it, his spoils are for him."" He said: I stood up, then said: ""Who will witness for me?"" Then I sat down. Then he said it a third time, so I stood up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What is the matter with you, O Abu Qatadah?"" He said: I recounted the story to him. A man from the people said: ""He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah, and the spoils of that slain person are with me. So please let him have them, O Messenger of Allah."" Abu Bakr said: ""No, by Allah, he will not give the spoils to you, leaving a lion from the lions of Allah who fights for Allah and His Messenger."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""He spoke the truth, so give it to him."" He gave it to me. I sold the armor and bought with it a palm grove in Banu Salimah, for it was the first wealth I acquired in Islam."
"1021.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"1022.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to do kaffara for a broken oath by feeding ten poor people. Each person got a mudd of wheat. He sometimes freed a slave if he had repeated the oath"
"1022.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to do kaffara for a broken oath by feeding ten poor people. Each person got a mudd of wheat. He sometimes freed a slave if he had repeated the oath"
"1023.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1023.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1024.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that one time the Messenger of Allah"
"1024.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that one time the Messenger of Allah"
"1025.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn Said from
Amr ibn Shuayb that when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him
and grant him peace, came back from Hunayn heading for al-Jiirrana,
the people crowded around so much to question him that his she-camel
backed into a tree, which became entangled in his cloak and pulled it
off his back. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant
him peace, said, ""Return my cloak to me. Are you afraid that I will
not distribute among you what Allah has given you as spoils. By He in
whose hand my self is! Had Allah given you spoils equal to the number
of acacia trees on the plain of Tihama, I would have distributed it
among you. You will not find me to be miserly, cowardly, or a liar.""
Then the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace,
got down and stood among the people, and said, ""Hand over even the
needle and thread, for stealing from the spoils is disgrace, fire,
ignominy on the Day of Rising for people who do it."" Then he took a
bit of camel fluff or something from the ground and said, ""By He in
whose hand my self is! What Allah has made spoils for you is not mine
- even the like of this! - except for the tax of one fifth, and the
tax of one fifth is returned to you."""
"1025.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"1026.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Uthman ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Khalda that Ibn Shihab had heard that Abu Lubaba ibn Abd al-Mundhir"
"1026.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Uthman ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Khalda that Ibn Shihab had heard that Abu Lubaba ibn Abd al-Mundhir"
"1027.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Musa from Mansur ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Hajabi from his mother that A'isha"
"1027.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Musa from Mansur ibn Abd ar-Rahman al-Hajabi from his mother that A'isha"
